      {
        "id": 174359,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-27T05:39:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Infinitor vs Young Legacy, O-X, Tachyon, and Nightmist in the Block</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Close game, overwhelming victory? &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>By the time we had removed half of Infinitor's health, he had decimated our team. &nbsp;Legacy, O-X, and Tachyon were dead, and Nightmist was at 1. &nbsp;But then Nightmist went into her Mistform. &nbsp;And at that point, we were all but guarenteed victory. &nbsp;I could have just stayed in Mistform and let him kill himself, but that wouldn't be fun. &nbsp;I healed back to full (courtesy of Starshield Necklace), and drew my entire deck, and stacked my trash with 4s. &nbsp;The Block guards were out in force, preventing the inmates from getting any toeholds. &nbsp;A few rounds later, and Infinitor was dead as a doornail.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Favorite moves:</p><p>There were two this game. &nbsp;The first was that the Block and Infinitor managed to work together to flip him back to his front side while Nightmist was in Mistform. &nbsp;That was entirely without the help of the heroes.</p><p>Secondly, the game ended after a massive Oblivion. &nbsp;I'd stacked two 4s, Elder Ring was out, and Young Legacy's incap had boosted my damage. &nbsp;Infinitor took 18 damage and nothing else survived (except Nightmist, who took no damage). &nbsp;Then Nighmist played Mistbound, and proceeded to kill Infinitor on the next round. &nbsp;Lockdown was in play, and the game ended with Infinitor totally locked down and controlled.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:57:42.566Z",
